<!doctype html>
<!--
  The front.

  This path answered 403 until 16 September 2026 — the host's default for a
  directory with nothing in it. It was a deliberate open question rather than an
  oversight (docs/WEBSITE.md), and the answer turned out to be forced from two
  directions at once: an App Store listing needs a support URL a reviewer can
  open, and a domain whose whole purpose is carrying links looks broken when the
  domain itself refuses to load.

  **It is built almost entirely out of words that already existed.** `tagline`
  and `about1`–`about3` were written for a `/s` with no seed in it, and a reader
  who types the domain is asking the same question as a reader who opens a spent
  link. They are commissioned in forty-one languages already; a front page
  written from scratch would have been a fresh commission in forty-two.

  Static, like every other page here: no analytics, no font CDN, no third-party
  anything.
-->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Peace Garden</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A plant grown from a meeting." />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/icon-180.png" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="pool" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <main class="page" id="page">
      <header class="masthead">
        <img class="mark" src="/assets/icon.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
        <span class="wordmark">Peace Garden</span>
      </header>

      <h1 class="heading" data-s="tagline"></h1>

      <section class="about">
        <p class="body" data-s="about1"></p>
        <p class="body" data-s="about2"></p>
        <p class="body" data-s="about3"></p>
      </section>

      <!--
        The three places this page can send somebody, in the order they become
        true for a reader: the garden is open now, the app is what you would
        install, and the Wild Fields is not running yet and says so.
      -->
      <section class="invitation">
        <h2 class="label" id="garden-title" data-s="gardenTitle"></h2>
        <p class="body" data-s="gardenBody"></p>
        <!--
          The ten area names are read out of `AREA_KEYS` rather than written
          here, so the list is in the reader's own language wherever the map
          already is. `plain.js` fills it.
        -->
        <p class="body quiet" id="areas"></p>
        <p>
          <!--
            Three links on this page carry the same word, which is one word rather
            than three commissions — but three links with the same name and three
            destinations is a list a screen reader cannot tell apart. The heading
            above each one is already the difference, so it is named as part of
            the link rather than written out again.
          -->
          <a
            class="quiet-button"
            href="/garden"
            id="garden-go"
            data-s="goOn"
            aria-labelledby="garden-go garden-title"
          ></a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="invitation">
        <h2 class="label" id="download-title" data-s="downloadTitle"></h2>
        <p class="body" data-s="downloadBody"></p>
        <p>
          <!--
            Three links on this page carry the same word, which is one word rather
            than three commissions — but three links with the same name and three
            destinations is a list a screen reader cannot tell apart. The heading
            above each one is already the difference, so it is named as part of
            the link rather than written out again.
          -->
          <a
            class="quiet-button"
            href="/download"
            id="download-go"
            data-s="goOn"
            aria-labelledby="download-go download-title"
          ></a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="invitation">
        <h2 class="label" id="wild-title" data-s="wildTitle"></h2>
        <p class="body" data-s="wildBody"></p>
        <p>
          <!--
            Three links on this page carry the same word, which is one word rather
            than three commissions — but three links with the same name and three
            destinations is a list a screen reader cannot tell apart. The heading
            above each one is already the difference, so it is named as part of
            the link rather than written out again.
          -->
          <a
            class="quiet-button"
            href="/wild"
            id="wild-go"
            data-s="goOn"
            aria-labelledby="wild-go wild-title"
          ></a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="notice body">
        <a href="/privacy" data-s="privacyTitle"></a>
      </p>

      <footer class="foot">
        <label class="chooser">
          <span class="label" id="language-label"></span>
          <span class="chooser__field">
            <select id="language" class="chooser__select"></select>
            <!-- Monoline, even weight, round free ends, per BRAND.md §3.2. -->
            <svg class="chooser__mark" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path
                d="M4 6.5 L8 10.5 L12 6.5"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.25"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/plain.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
